Package: batman-adv-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: dkms (>= 3.0), ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: linux-headers-amd64 | linux-headers-generic
Description: B.A.T.M.A.N. advanced kernel module sources (DKMS)
 batman-adv is a Layer 2 mesh routing protocol implemented as an
 out-of-tree Linux kernel module. This package ships the module
 sources and registers them with DKMS, so the module is compiled
 automatically whenever a new kernel image is installed.
 .
 No prebuilt module is included; DKMS builds it on the target host
 against the running kernel's headers. Install the linux-headers-*
 package matching your kernel to enable the build.
